Hello World!

Firecrawl example
-----------------

A tiny "Hello World" for Firecrawl (https://docs.firecrawl.dev): run a small
crawl (capped at 5 pages by default) and print the title and URL of each page
found, using the official Firecrawl Python SDK. Override the page cap with the
CRAWL_LIMIT environment variable (e.g. CRAWL_LIMIT=3).

Setup:

    pip install -r requirements.txt
    cp .env.example .env    # add your FIRECRAWL_API_KEY, or export it directly

Run (defaults to https://example.com; pass any URL as an argument):

    python hello_firecrawl.py
    python hello_firecrawl.py https://firecrawl.dev
    CRAWL_LIMIT=3 python hello_firecrawl.py    # crawl at most 3 pages

Get an API key at https://www.firecrawl.dev and read the docs at
https://docs.firecrawl.dev
